messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "Global renewable energy share surpasses coal for electricity generation.",
      "detail": "Solar and wind become the dominant new power sources due to falling costs and policy momentum."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "First widespread commercial deployment of autonomous freight trucks.",
      "detail": "Long-haul logistics transitions rapidly, reducing costs but displacing millions of drivers."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "CRISPR-based therapies cure common inherited blood disorders.",
      "detail": "Sickle cell and beta-thalassemia become routinely treatable in advanced health systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Global fertility rate falls below replacement in most regions.",
      "detail": "Sub-Saharan Africa remains the only major region with fertility above replacement, while aging accelerates elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "Lab-grown meat reaches price parity with conventional meat.",
      "detail": "Cultivated protein becomes common in processed foods and fast food, reducing livestock emissions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "First permanent lunar research station is established.",
      "detail": "A multinational consortium maintains a continuously crewed base, focused on astronomy and resource prospecting."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Global population peaks around 9.3 billion.",
      "detail": "Aging, urbanization, and education drive the peak earlier than previously forecast, followed by slow decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Direct air capture of CO2 becomes cost-competitive.",
      "detail": "Large-scale facilities remove billions of tonnes annually, though deployment remains far below needed levels for decades."
    },
    {
      "year": 2054,
      "event": "First human crew reaches Mars orbit.",
      "detail": "A short orbital mission with no landing, but it proves long-duration deep-space life support."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Universal basic income is implemented in most wealthy nations.",
      "detail": "Automation-driven unemployment and political pressure lead to broad adoption of unconditional cash transfers."
    },
    {
      "year": 2067,
      "event": "First child born after full artificial womb gestation.",
      "detail": "Ectogenesis becomes viable for premature infants, later extended to full-term pregnancies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global sea level has risen by 50 cm since 2020.",
      "detail": "Major coastal cities invest heavily in sea walls and managed retreat, but some low-lying islands become uninhabitable."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Fusion power plants provide reliable baseload electricity in several countries.",
      "detail": "The first commercial fusion reactors are expensive but begin to displace natural gas in industrial grids."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Widespread neural implants restore movement and hearing.",
      "detail": "Brain-computer interfaces become standard for paralysis and sensory loss, with early consumer cognitive enhancement."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Average global temperature is about 2.5°C above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Despite massive mitigation, the world faces severe heat stress, biodiversity loss, and agricultural shifts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "First permanent Martian settlement is established.",
      "detail": "A small self-sustaining colony of a few thousand people exists, dependent on Earth for high-tech equipment."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Human lifespan routinely extends beyond 100 years in developed regions.",
      "detail": "Senolytics, epigenetic reprogramming, and organ replacement make centenarians common."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Language becomes increasingly unified through real-time neural translation.",
      "detail": "Spoken language barriers effectively vanish, though cultural and literary languages persist."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Climate refugees exceed one billion cumulative since 2020.",
      "detail": "Drought, sea-level rise, and heat make parts of South Asia, the Middle East, and Central America barely habitable."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Asteroid mining begins delivering platinum-group metals to Earth orbit.",
      "detail": "It does not crash Earth markets due to regulation and high launch costs, but enables orbital construction."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Genetic enhancement of human embryos becomes common in wealthy nations.",
      "detail": "Disease resistance and cognitive traits are selected, creating widespread ethical and social divides."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Earth's population stabilizes around 4 billion.",
      "detail": "A long decline driven by low fertility and high longevity leads to a much older, but smaller, human population."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "The Antarctic ice sheet has lost one-third of its mass.",
      "detail": "Global sea level is now 6 meters higher, permanently reshaping coastlines and river deltas."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Human settlements exist on the Moon, Mars, and several large asteroids.",
      "detail": "Total off-Earth population is around 2 million, with a self-sustaining economy based on energy and materials."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "A large solar storm severely damages Earth's power grids and satellites.",
      "detail": "Recovery takes a decade and accelerates a shift toward decentralized, hardened energy systems."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Brain emulation and digital consciousness are achieved for short periods.",
      "detail": "Technology exists to scan and simulate a human brain, but continuity of self is uncertain and subject to intense debate."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Earth's biosphere is partially restored through massive geoengineering.",
      "detail": "Reforestation, ocean fertilization, and genetic de-extinction return many lost species, though ecosystems are heavily managed."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Human languages have evolved into several mutually unintelligible off-world branches.",
      "detail": "Mars and lunar colonists have distinct dialects and cultural identities from Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Interstellar probes reach nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "Uncrewed craft send back data from Alpha Centauri, Barnard's Star, and other nearby systems after centuries of travel."
    },
    {
      "year": 5500,
      "event": "A major volcanic supereruption causes a decade of global cooling.",
      "detail": "Crop failures and migration stress human systems, but off-world colonies provide some buffer."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Human population in the solar system reaches 10 billion.",
      "detail": "Most people still live on Earth, but orbital habitats and Mars hold significant populations."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "Earth's climate has been stabilized at about 1.5°C above preindustrial.",
      "detail": "Carbon removal over centuries and a smaller human footprint allow gradual cooling from peak warming."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "The first self-sustaining human colony outside the solar system is planned.",
      "detail": "A generation ship is under construction, designed for a journey of several thousand years to a nearby star."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "Digital and biological human lineages become distinct cultural groups.",
      "detail": "Some humans exist primarily as digital consciousness, while others remain biological, leading to separate political entities."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Earth's surface has been significantly re-wilded.",
      "detail": "Large areas previously used for agriculture are returned to forests and grasslands due to vertical farming and synthetic food."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "The first generation ship leaves the solar system.",
      "detail": "Carrying several thousand humans in cryogenic and biological states, it begins a multi-millennium journey."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity is a multi-planet, partly digital civilization.",
      "detail": "Earth remains the cultural homeworld, but human existence is spread across the solar system with outposts moving toward other stars."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity survives the next eight millennia, though not without severe climate disruption, population decline, and social upheaval in the coming centuries. Technological progress, off-world settlement, and eventual climate stabilization allow a smaller but enduring multi-planet civilization. By 10000, humans exist in both biological and digital forms, concentrated on Earth, the Moon, Mars, and a few space habitats, with the first true interstellar journey underway."
}
